<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ========================================================================
     DROIDWORKS_PRIMITIVE_TIER_1 (packet B9). Ruling 8, verbatim: "Modules:
     Basically loot-only forever. They CAN be fabricated, but at a grossly
     inferior level. The G2 repair droid is an example of what they can make
     entirely by themselves (except for the brain, which they can't do at
     all ever). Very primitive." G2 = the goose-necked Phantom Menace-style
     repair droid: exposed cabling, tube-and-plate frame, twin lamp-eye
     photoreceptors on a stalk neck, claw hands, three-toed feet.

     HAND-AUTHORED, deliberately NOT emitted by
     Source/gen_droidworks_defs.py. That generator classifies donor-mod
     races into the 7 CHASSIS_PLAN families by reading extraction.json
     (OuterRimDroidDepot/KotORDroids/JDS_Separatists) - there is no donor
     race for "Primitive" (it is Jawa-built junk, not absorbed from another
     mod), so it cannot be derived the way Races_Families.xml's 7 abstracts
     are, and does NOT belong in that generator-owned file (which is
     re-written wholesale on every run and would silently drop a hand-added
     8th family). This file is Races_Families.xml's sibling for exactly the
     one family with no donor to absorb - same relationship Races_Base.xml
     already has to that generator (its own docstring: "hand-authored... not
     regenerated here").

     DW_Family_Primitive = chassisClass 7 (0 labour, 1 protocol, 2 astromech,
     3 battle, 4 heavy, 5 probe, 6 power - DroidworksExtension's own
     comment, extended here). Differentiator per the item's own design
     guidance: baseHealthScale 0.6, below every other family's 0.7-1.5 range
     (Races_Families.xml) - "grossly inferior" reads as structurally
     fragile, not merely weaker in the fine-parts sense (that's the
     ~40%-of-donor axis, Parts_Droidworks_Primitive.xml). powerFallPerDay
     0.6 (crude power management - worse than Labour's 0.33, better than a
     combat droid's constant 1.0 since the G2 isn't fighting).
     energyDensity 0 at the family level: neither chassis explodes by
     default - the Junker race below raises its own to 3, same
     DroidworksExtension full-restate pattern Races_JDS.xml's own B1 Battle
     Droid block already uses (XML list-inheritance APPENDS modExtensions,
     so the race's own block must restate every field, not just the deltas
     - CompDroidDetonation.cs's own header explains why LastOrDefault reads
     correctly off that).
======================================================================== -->
<Defs>

  <AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace Name="DW_Family_Primitive" ParentName="DW_Race_Base" Abstract="True">
    <race>
      <baseBodySize>0.7</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.6</baseHealthScale>
    </race>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.DroidworksExtension">
        <powerFallPerDay>0.6</powerFallPerDay>
        <energyDensity>0</energyDensity>
        <chassisClass>7</chassisClass>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       RSW_DW_Race_Primitive_G2Unit — "the one chassis the Jawa build whole"
       (§1.3). 🔴 FIXED live 2026-09-08 (full-list confirming load): the
       original defName RSW_DW_Race_Primitive_G2 ("...G2") logged "Config
       error... ends with a numerical digit, which is not allowed on
       ThingDefs" - a real vanilla ThingDef constraint, not caught by
       validate_patch.py or a build. Renamed with a letter suffix; no other
       def references the old name (DroidAssembly.KindForHeadDef keys off
       RSW_DW_Head_Primitive and the PawnKindDef, never the race defName
       directly).
       Frame, limbs, sensors, claws all Primitive-tier
       (Parts_Droidworks_Primitive.xml); the head/brain is still the SAME
       imported-brain economy every other family uses (ruling 6 - "the
       brain, which they can't do at all ever" is universal, not
       Primitive-specific), so RSW_DW_Head_Primitive (Heads_Droidworks.xml)
       is just an eighth family casing around the same trio, not a new
       mechanic.

       🔶 PLACEHOLDER ART, not the real G2. New sprite art (goose neck, twin
       lamp-eye photoreceptors on a stalk, claw hands, three-toed feet,
       exposed cabling per the design doc) needs the owner's own eye
       (generating-rimworld-sprites skill; CLAUDE.md's "iterate by
       LOOKING") and is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE for this packet - a parent
       session handles it separately. Body art reused verbatim from
       OuterRimDroidDepot's own DUM repair-droid texture (OuterRim/Droid/DUM,
       already active in this mod via Races_OuterRim.xml's own
       RSW_DW_Race_OuterRim_DUMDroid) - same "reuse an active mod's art by
       texPath" convention Items_Droidworks.xml's RSW_DW_DroidHead already
       established, picked because DUM is the closest existing shape to "a
       small bipedal repair droid" this mod ships. colorChannels copied
       verbatim from that same DUM block so the reused texture's palette
       renders correctly (RGBA(112,68,55,255), a rust-brown that also reads
       as "junk", pending the real G2 palette).
  ======================================================================== -->
  <AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace ParentName="DW_Family_Primitive">
    <defName>RSW_DW_Race_Primitive_G2Unit</defName>
    <label>G2 repair droid</label>
    <description>A goose-necked repair droid the Jawa built whole - tube-and-plate frame, claw hands, three-toed feet, exposed cabling, twin lamp-eye photoreceptors on a stalk neck. Every part but the brain is their own crude work.</description>
    <race>
      <baseBodySize>0.75</baseBodySize>
    </race>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.2</MoveSpeed>
    </statBases>
    <alienRace>
      <graphicPaths>
        <skinShader>Cutout</skinShader>
        <body>
          <path>OuterRim/Droid/DUM</path>
        </body>
      </graphicPaths>
      <generalSettings>
        <alienPartGenerator>
          <headTypes Inherit="False">
            <li>RSW_DW_HeadType_Blank</li>
          </headTypes>
          <bodyTypes Inherit="False">
            <li>Male</li>
          </bodyTypes>
          <colorChannels Inherit="False">
            <li>
              <name>skin</name>
              <first Class="ColorGenerator_Options">
                <options>
                  <li>
                    <weight>100</weight>
                    <only>RGBA(112,68,55,255)</only>
                  </li>
                </options>
              </first>
              <second Class="ColorGenerator_Options">
                <options>
                  <li>
                    <weight>100</weight>
                    <only>RGBA(112,68,55,255)</only>
                  </li>
                </options>
              </second>
            </li>
          </colorChannels>
        </alienPartGenerator>
      </generalSettings>
    </alienRace>
  </AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       RSW_DW_Race_Primitive_Junker — ruling 2, verbatim: "Junkers might have
       one or two atrocious, clumsy droids spewing fire and able to blow
       themselves up against the enemy or their structures." Maps onto the
       EXISTING CompDroidDetonation mechanic (state 5, already live on 21
       races) rather than a new explosion system - energyDensity 3 matches
       DW_Family_Power's own tuning (Races_Families.xml, the Gonk precedent),
       deliberateDenyModule true matches the JDS Battle-family "deny-your-
       parts" precedent (CompDroidDetonation.cs's own header quotes
       droid_system_build_spec.md: "Deliberate deny-your-parts modules and
       Gonk/KX-12 nature raise density").

       🔶 PLACEHOLDER ART. Body art reused verbatim from OuterRimDroidDepot's
       MSE mouse-droid texture (OuterRim/Droid/MSE, already active via
       Races_OuterRim.xml's RSW_DW_Race_OuterRim_MSEDroid) - small, boxy,
       crude-looking, the closest existing shape to "a junk-built firebomb
       on legs". Not this packet's art deliverable (only the G2 gets a
       named new-art obligation in the design doc); reused per the same
       convention as G2 above.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace ParentName="DW_Family_Primitive">
    <defName>RSW_DW_Race_Primitive_Junker</defName>
    <label>Junker suicide droid</label>
    <description>An atrocious, clumsy droid the Junkers scrap together out of whatever they have and rig to blow. It spews fire and throws itself at the enemy, or their structures, whichever it reaches first.</description>
    <race>
      <baseBodySize>0.6</baseBodySize>
    </race>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.8</MoveSpeed>
    </statBases>
    <alienRace>
      <graphicPaths>
        <skinShader>Cutout</skinShader>
        <body>
          <path>OuterRim/Droid/MSE</path>
        </body>
      </graphicPaths>
      <generalSettings>
        <alienPartGenerator>
          <headTypes Inherit="False">
            <li>RSW_DW_HeadType_Blank</li>
          </headTypes>
          <bodyTypes Inherit="False">
            <li>Male</li>
          </bodyTypes>
        </alienPartGenerator>
      </generalSettings>
    </alienRace>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.DroidworksExtension">
        <powerFallPerDay>0.6</powerFallPerDay>
        <energyDensity>3</energyDensity>
        <chassisClass>7</chassisClass>
        <deliberateDenyModule>true</deliberateDenyModule>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <comps>
      <!-- CompDroidDetonation, same rollout convention Races_JDS.xml's own
           B1 Battle Droid block documents: every energyDensity>0 race gets
           this, per its own race's DroidworksExtension tuning. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.CompProperties_DroidDetonation" />
    </comps>
  </AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace>

</Defs>
